srow(309, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"IS HE NOT YOUR FATHER WHO ACQUIRED YOU?" — SHIMON BEN CHALAFTA SAYS: IF THE WEAK WERE ABOVE AND THE STRONG BELOW, WHO WINS? COULD YOU PREVAIL? HOW MUCH MORE WHEN THE STRONG IS ABOVE AND THE WEAK BELOW; "BE NOT RASH WITH YOUR MOUTH … FOR GOD IS IN HEAVEN AND YOU ON EARTH" (Ecclesiastes 5:1). ({SP_(309, 4, "שאם", "היה", "חלש", "מלמעלה", "וגבור", "מלמטה")} "if the weak were above and the strong below"; {SP_(309, 4, "מי", "נוצח")} "who wins"): the wrestlers\' a-fortiori (I1); the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-02). Fresh.')
srow(309, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IS HE NOT YOUR FATHER WHO ACQUIRED YOU?" — MOSES SAID TO ISRAEL: YOU ARE BELOVED TO HIM, YOU ARE HIS ACQUISITION, YOU ARE NOT HIS INHERITANCE. A PARABLE: ONE WHOSE FATHER LEFT HIM TEN FIELDS, AND HE BOUGHT ONE FIELD OF HIS OWN AND LOVED IT MORE THAN ALL HIS FATHER LEFT HIM; SO ONE LEFT TEN PALACES WHO BOUGHT ONE OF HIS OWN. SO MOSES TO ISRAEL: YOU ARE BELOVED, HIS ACQUISITION, NOT HIS INHERITANCE. ({SP_(309, 5, "חביבים", "אתם", "לו", "קנין", "אתם", "לו")} "you are beloved to Him, you are His acquisition"; {SP_(309, 5, "ואי", "אתם", "ירושה", "לו")} "and you are not His inheritance"): ACQUISITION AGAINST INHERITANCE — the bought field loved above the inherited ten (the compiled inheritance law\'s two titles on the tape); the compile: Israel\'s status as acquired (kinyan), a reference to 32:9\'s portion; no law (DV32-02). Fresh.')
srow(309, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO ACQUIRED YOU" — ONE OF THREE CALLED THE ACQUISITION OF THE PLACE: THE TORAH — "THE LORD ACQUIRED ME AT THE BEGINNING OF HIS WAY" (Proverbs 8:22); ISRAEL — "IS HE NOT YOUR FATHER WHO ACQUIRED YOU"; THE TEMPLE — "THIS MOUNTAIN WHICH HIS RIGHT HAND ACQUIRED" (Psalm 78:54). ({SP_(309, 6, "זה", "אחד", "משלשה", "שנקראו", "קנין", "למקום")} "this is one of three called the acquisition of the Place"; {SP_(309, 6, "בית", "המקדש", "נקרא", "קנין", "למקום")} "the Temple is called the acquisition of the Place"): THE THREE ACQUISITIONS (the Torah, Israel, the Temple — Mishnah Avot 6:10 the parallel with five, cited; the Mekhilta on Exodus 15:16 the parallel); the Writings\' seats cited, never read; the compile: a word\'s three seats, no law (DV32-02). Fresh.')
srow(309, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE MADE YOU AND ESTABLISHED YOU" — R. MEIR USED TO SAY: A CITY THAT HAS EVERYTHING IN IT — PRIESTS FROM IT, PROPHETS FROM IT, SAGES FROM IT, SCRIBES FROM IT: "OUT OF HIM THE CORNERSTONE, OUT OF HIM THE PEG" (Zechariah 10:4); R. YEHUDAH SAYS: HE MADE YOU HOLLOWS UPON HOLLOWS (kavin); R. SHIMON BEN YEHUDAH SAYS: HE SET YOU ON YOUR BASE, FED YOU THE SPOIL OF SEVEN NATIONS, GAVE YOU WHAT HE SWORE TO YOU, MADE YOU INHERIT WHAT HE PROMISED; R. DOSTAI BEN YEHUDAH SAYS: HE MADE YOU CHAMBERS UPON CHAMBERS WITHIN — IF ONE ROSE ON ITS FELLOW YOU COULD NOT STAND. ({SP_(309, 7, "כרכא", "דכולא", "ביה")} "a city that has everything in it — the Aramaic saying"; {SP_(309, 7, "כהנים", "מתוכו", "נביאים", "מתוכו", "חכמים", "מתוכו", "סופרים")} "priests from it, prophets from it, sages from it, scribes"; {SP_(309, 7, "הלעיטך", "בזת", "שבעה", "עממים")} "fed you the spoil of seven nations"): FOUR READINGS OF "ESTABLISHED" — the whole city, the body\'s conduits, the seven nations\' spoil (7:1\'s seven on the tape, the oath and the promise kept — a RUN CITATION of the tape\'s statuses), the body\'s chambers (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-02). Fresh.')
srow(310, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"REMEMBER THE DAYS OF OLD" (32:7) — HE SAID TO THEM: REMEMBER WHAT I DID TO THE FIRST GENERATIONS — TO THE GENERATION OF THE FLOOD, TO THE GENERATION OF THE DISPERSION, TO THE MEN OF SODOM. The head row of piska 310 ({SP_(310, 1, "הזכרו", "מה", "שעשיתי", "לדורות", "הראשונים")} "remember what I did to the first generations"): the three judgments named (the tape\'s own entries — RUN CITATIONS: Genesis 6-8, 11, 19); the compile: the song\'s "remember" a call to the recorded past — no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"CONSIDER THE YEARS OF GENERATION AND GENERATION" — THERE IS NO GENERATION WITHOUT MEN LIKE THE GENERATION OF THE FLOOD, NONE WITHOUT MEN LIKE SODOM — BUT EACH ONE IS JUDGED BY HIS DEEDS. ({SP_(310, 2, "אין", "לך", "דור", "שאין", "בו", "כאנשי", "דור")} "there is no generation without men like the generation"; {SP_(310, 2, "שנדון", "כל", "אחד", "ואחד", "לפי", "מעשיו")} "that each and every one is judged by his deeds"): judgment by the person, not the generation (24:16\'s rule on the tape); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"ASK YOUR FATHER AND HE WILL DECLARE TO YOU" — THESE ARE THE PROPHETS: "AND ELISHA SAW AND CRIED: MY FATHER, MY FATHER" (2 Kings 2:12). ({SP_(310, 3, "אלו", "נביאים")} "these are the prophets"): the father the prophet; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR ELDERS AND THEY WILL TELL YOU" — THESE ARE THE ELDERS: "GATHER ME SEVENTY MEN OF THE ELDERS OF ISRAEL" (Numbers 11:16). ({SP_(310, 4, "אלו", "זקנים")} "these are the elders"): the elders the seventy (the tape\'s own count at Numbers 11:16 — a RUN CITATION; the Sanhedrin the translator\'s gloss); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "REMEMBER THE DAYS OF OLD" — HE SAID TO THEM: WHENEVER THE HOLY ONE BRINGS SUFFERINGS UPON YOU, REMEMBER HOW MUCH GOOD AND CONSOLATION HE WILL GIVE YOU IN THE WORLD TO COME. ({SP_(310, 5, "כל", "זמן", "שהקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא", "מביא", "עליכם")} "whenever the Holy One, blessed be He, brings upon you"): the days of old read as the days of the world to come (olam both); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"CONSIDER THE YEARS OF GENERATION AND GENERATION" — THIS IS THE GENERATION OF THE MESSIAH, WHICH HAS THREE GENERATIONS: "THEY SHALL FEAR YOU WITH THE SUN AND BEFORE THE MOON, GENERATION OF GENERATIONS" (Psalm 72:5). ({SP_(310, 6, "זה", "דורו", "של", "משיח", "שיש", "בו", "שלשה")} "this is the generation of the Messiah, which has three"): the plural counted as three (the Mekhilta on Amalek the parallel, cited); the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"ASK YOUR FATHER AND HE WILL DECLARE TO YOU" — TOMORROW ISRAEL WILL SEE AND HEAR AS THOSE WHO HEAR FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE: "YOUR EARS SHALL HEAR A WORD BEHIND YOU, SAYING" (Isaiah 30:21), "YOUR TEACHER SHALL NO MORE BE HIDDEN, YOUR EYES SHALL SEE YOUR TEACHER" (Isaiah 30:20). ({SP_(310, 7, "למחר", "עתידים", "ישראל", "להיות", "רואים", "ושומעים")} "tomorrow Israel will see and hear"): the father the Holy One in the future; the Prophets\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(310, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR ELDERS AND THEY WILL TELL YOU" — WHAT I SHOWED THE ELDERS ON THE MOUNTAIN: "AND TO MOSES HE SAID: COME UP TO THE LORD" (Exodus 24:1). ({SP_(310, 8, "מה", "שהראיתי", "לזקנים", "בהר")} "what I showed the elders on the mountain"): the elders\' vision at Sinai (Exodus 24:1, 9-11 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(311, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" (32:8) — BEFORE ABRAHAM OUR FATHER CAME THE HOLY ONE, AS IT WERE, JUDGED THE WORLD BY THE MEASURE OF CRUELTY: THE MEN OF THE FLOOD SINNED — HE FLOATED THEM LIKE SPARKS ON THE WATER; THE MEN OF THE TOWER — HE SCATTERED THEM FROM ONE END OF THE WORLD TO THE OTHER; THE MEN OF SODOM — HE SWEPT THEM WITH BRIMSTONE AND FIRE; BUT WHEN ABRAHAM CAME INTO THE WORLD HE MERITED TO RECEIVE SUFFERINGS, AND THEY BEGAN TO COME ON: "AND THERE WAS A FAMINE IN THE LAND, AND ABRAM WENT DOWN TO EGYPT" (Genesis 12:10); AND IF YOU SAY, WHY DO SUFFERINGS COME? FOR THE LOVE OF ISRAEL — "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES BY THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL". The head row of piska 311 ({SP_(311, 1, "היה", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא", "דן", "את", "העולם")} "the Holy One, blessed be He, judged the world"; {SP_(311, 1, "במדת", "אכזריות")} "by the measure of cruelty"; {SP_(311, 1, "מפני", "חבתם", "של", "ישראל")} "for the love of Israel"): THE TURN AT ABRAHAM — catastrophe before him, chastisement after (Genesis 12:10\'s famine the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of the call); the compile: the world\'s judgment mode a status that changes at Abraham\'s entry (the tape\'s own entries — the Flood, Babel, Sodom, the famine: RUN CITATIONS); no law (DV32-03). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_27_the_call\'s reading — Genesis 12:10).')
srow(311, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" — WHEN THE HOLY ONE GAVE THE WORLD TO THE NATIONS HE MARKED THE BORDER OF EACH NATION SO THEY WOULD NOT BE MIXED: HE SENT THE SONS OF GOMER TO GOMER, OF MAGOG TO MAGOG, OF MADAI TO MADAI, OF JAVAN TO JAVAN, OF TUBAL TO TUBAL; HE MARKED THE NATIONS\' BORDERS SO THEY WOULD NOT ENTER THE LAND OF ISRAEL — "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES". ({SP_(311, 2, "פרש", "תחומה", "של", "כל", "אמה", "ואמה")} "He marked the border of each and every nation"; {SP_(311, 2, "כדי", "שלא", "יכנסו", "לארץ", "ישראל")} "so that they would not enter the land of Israel"): Genesis 10:2\'s sons of Japheth as the boundary list (the tape\'s own table of nations — a RUN CITATION); the compile: the nations\' borders a status of the world, no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(311, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" — WHEN THE HOLY ONE GAVE THE TORAH TO ISRAEL HE STOOD AND LOOKED AND CONSIDERED: "HE STOOD AND MEASURED THE EARTH, HE LOOKED AND MADE THE NATIONS TREMBLE" (Habakkuk 3:6) — AND THERE WAS NO NATION FIT TO RECEIVE THE TORAH BUT ISRAEL — "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES". ({SP_(311, 3, "ולא", "היתה", "אמה", "באמות", "שהיתה", "ראויה", "לקבל")} "and there was no nation among the nations fit to receive"): the Torah offered and the nations measured (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(311, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" — WHEN HE GAVE THE WORLD TO THE NATIONS HE ALLOTTED THEM GEHENNA: "THERE IS ASSYRIA AND ALL HER COMPANY" (Ezekiel 32:22), "THERE THE PRINCES OF THE NORTH AND ALL THE SIDONIANS" (32:30), "THERE EDOM, HER KINGS" (32:29); AND IF YOU SAY, WHO TAKES THEIR WEALTH AND HONOR? SAY: ISRAEL — "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES". ({SP_(311, 4, "חלקם", "בגיהנם")} "He allotted them Gehenna"; {SP_(311, 4, "מי", "נוטל", "עשרם", "וכבודם", "של", "אלו")} "who takes the wealth and honor of these"): the nations\' portion below and Israel\'s above (the Prophets\' seats cited, never read); no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(311, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN THE MOST HIGH GAVE THE NATIONS THEIR INHERITANCE" — WHEN THE HOLY ONE GAVE OF THE NATIONS THEIR SIN-FEARING AND FIT ONES; "WHEN HE SEPARATED THE CHILDREN OF MEN" — THIS IS THE GENERATION OF THE DISPERSION: "AND FROM THERE THE LORD SCATTERED THEM" (Genesis 11:9); "HE SET THE BORDERS OF THE PEOPLES" — R. ELIEZER SON OF R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAYS: IT SAYS "SIXTY ARE THE QUEENS AND EIGHTY THE CONCUBINES" (Song of Songs 6:8) — SIXTY AND EIGHTY ARE A HUNDRED AND FORTY; OUR FATHERS WENT DOWN TO EGYPT WITH ONLY SEVENTY SOULS: "WITH SEVENTY SOULS YOUR FATHERS WENT DOWN" (10:22); AND IT SAYS "BORDERS (gevulot) OF THE PEOPLES" — NOT "BORDER OF THE PEOPLES" IS WRITTEN BUT "BORDERS": THE NATIONS MERITED TO TAKE TWO PORTIONS BY THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL. ({SP_(311, 5, "זה", "דור", "הפלגה")} "this is the generation of the Dispersion"; {SP_(311, 5, "ששים", "ושמנים", "הרי", "מאה", "וארבעים")} "sixty and eighty — behold a hundred and forty"; {SP_(311, 5, "גבולי", "עמים", "אין", "כתוב", "כאן", "אלא", "גבלת")} "border of the peoples is not written here but borders"; {SP_(311, 5, "זכו", "אמות", "לטול", "שני", "חלקים")} "the nations merited to take two portions"): THE NUMBER OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL COMPUTED — seventy (10:22 the seat that read this row at chapter 10; Genesis 46:27 and Exodus 1:5 the tape\'s own count) against a hundred and forty nations (60 + 80, the Writings\' seat cited): the plural "borders" read as two each — an arithmetic the compile can check on the tape\'s own figures (the seventy on the ledger; the hundred and forty the shelf\'s); Genesis 11:9\'s scattering the Genesis seats that read this row (Babel, the separation); no law (DV32-03). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 10\'s reading — 10:22; the Genesis ledgers gen_25_babel and gen_29_separation_promise — Genesis 11:9).')
srow(312, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE PORTION OF THE LORD IS HIS PEOPLE" (32:9) — A PARABLE OF A KING WHO HAD A FIELD AND GAVE IT TO TENANTS; THE TENANTS BEGAN TO STEAL FROM IT — HE TOOK IT FROM THEM AND GAVE IT TO THEIR SONS; THEY WERE WORSE THAN THE FIRST — HE GAVE IT TO THEIR SONS\' SONS; THEY WERE WORSE STILL; A SON WAS BORN TO HIM — HE SAID: GO OUT OF MINE, I WILL NOT HAVE YOU IN IT; GIVE ME MY PORTION THAT I MAY KNOW IT. SO WHEN ABRAHAM CAME, DROSS WENT OUT OF HIM — ISHMAEL AND THE SONS OF KETURAH; ISAAC — ESAU AND THE CHIEFS OF EDOM; WORSE THAN THE FIRST; BUT WHEN JACOB CAME NO DROSS WENT OUT OF HIM — ALL HIS SONS WERE BORN FIT: "AND JACOB WAS A PERFECT MAN, DWELLING IN TENTS" (Genesis 25:27). FROM WHERE DOES THE PLACE KNOW HIS PORTION? FROM JACOB — "JACOB THE LOT OF HIS INHERITANCE", "FOR THE LORD CHOSE JACOB FOR HIMSELF" (Psalm 135:4); STILL THE MATTER HANGS — DID THE HOLY ONE CHOOSE JACOB OR JACOB THE HOLY ONE? "ISRAEL FOR HIS TREASURE"; STILL IT HANGS — "AND THE LORD YOUR GOD CHOSE YOU TO BE A TREASURED PEOPLE" (14:2); AND WHENCE THAT JACOB TOO CHOSE HIM? "NOT LIKE THESE IS THE PORTION OF JACOB" (Jeremiah 10:16). The head row of piska 312 ({SP_(312, 1, "משל", "למלך", "שהיה", "לו", "שדה", "ונתנה", "לעריסים")} "a parable of a king who had a field and gave it to tenants"; {SP_(312, 1, "מהיכן", "המקום", "מכיר", "את", "חלקו")} "from where does the Place know His portion"; {SP_(312, 1, "ועדין", "הדבר", "תלוי", "בדלא", "תלוי")} "and still the matter hangs on what is not settled"): THE PORTION TRACED TO JACOB — three generations of tenants (Abraham\'s and Isaac\'s dross, Jacob\'s twelve fit sons: the tape\'s own genealogy, RUN CITATIONS), then the chooser settled by 14:2 (the seat that read this row at chapter 14 — the treasured people compiled there) and Jacob\'s own choice by Jeremiah; the compile: the_lords_people status seated at Jacob, both directions of the choice (DV32-03); the Writings\' and the Prophets\' seats cited, never read. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 14\'s reading — 14:2).')
srow(312, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"JACOB THE CORD (chevel) OF HIS INHERITANCE" — CORD IS ONLY LOT: "THE LOTS HAVE FALLEN TO ME IN PLEASANT PLACES" (Psalm 16:6), "AND THE LOTS OF MANASSEH FELL TEN" (Joshua 17:5), "OUT OF THE LOT OF THE CHILDREN OF JUDAH THE INHERITANCE OF SIMEON" (Joshua 19:9). ANOTHER WORD: AS THIS CORD IS THREEFOLD, SO JACOB WAS THE THIRD OF THE FATHERS AND RECEIVED THE REWARD OF ALL: WHEN ABRAHAM WAS BORN — "A BROTHER IS BORN FOR ADVERSITY" (Proverbs 17:17); ISAAC — "TWO ARE BETTER THAN ONE" (Ecclesiastes 4:9); JACOB — "THE THREEFOLD CORD IS NOT QUICKLY BROKEN" (Ecclesiastes 4:12). ({SP_(312, 2, "אין", "חבל", "אלא", "גורל")} "cord is only lot"; {SP_(312, 2, "מה", "חבל", "זה", "משלש")} "as this cord is threefold"; {SP_(312, 2, "כך", "היה", "יעקב", "שלישי", "לאבות")} "so Jacob was the third of the fathers"): the cord as the lot (Onkelos: adav, the lot — the measure) and as the three strands; the Hebrew carries a bracketed "and it says" (an editor\'s supplement in the export); the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-03). Fresh.')
srow(313, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE FOUND HIM IN A DESERT LAND" (32:10) — THIS IS ABRAHAM. A PARABLE OF A KING WHO WENT OUT WITH HIS TROOPS TO THE DESERT; HIS TROOPS LEFT HIM IN A PLACE OF TROUBLES, OF RAIDERS, OF BANDITS, AND WENT; ONE WARRIOR WAS APPOINTED TO HIM: MY LORD KING, LET NOT YOUR HEART FAIL, FEAR NOTHING — BY YOUR LIFE I WILL NOT LEAVE YOU UNTIL YOU ENTER YOUR PALACE AND SLEEP IN YOUR BED — "AND HE SAID TO HIM: I AM THE LORD WHO BROUGHT YOU OUT OF UR OF THE CHALDEES" (Genesis 15:7). The head row of piska 313 ({SP_(313, 1, "זה", "אברהם")} "this is Abraham"; {SP_(313, 1, "חייך", "שאיני", "מניחך", "עד", "שתכנס", "לפלטרים", "שלך")} "by your life, I will not leave you until you enter your palace"): THE FIRST OF FOUR READINGS OF THE VERSE — Abraham found (313:1-4), Israel at Sinai (313:5-9), Israel in the desert (313:10-13), the future (313:14-16); Genesis 15:7 the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of the covenant of the pieces; THE ENGLISH MISPRINTS THE SEAT (Genesis 16:7 for the Hebrew\'s 15:7 — the Hebrew\'s marker true); the compile: no law (DV32-04). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_31_covenant_pieces\' reading — Genesis 15:7).')
srow(313, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE COMPASSED HIM ABOUT" — AS IT SAYS "AND THE LORD SAID TO ABRAM: GO FROM YOUR LAND" (Genesis 12:1). ({SP_(313, 2, "יסבבנהו", "כענין", "שנאמר")} "He compassed him about — as it is said"): the compassing Abraham\'s journey (Genesis 12:1 the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of the call — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-04). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_27_the_call\'s reading — Genesis 12:1).')
srow(313, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE CARED FOR HIM (yevonenehu — gave him understanding)" — BEFORE ABRAHAM OUR FATHER CAME THE HOLY ONE, AS IT WERE, WAS KING OVER THE HEAVENS ALONE: "THE LORD, GOD OF HEAVEN, WHO TOOK ME" (Genesis 24:7); BUT WHEN ABRAHAM CAME HE MADE HIM KING OVER HEAVEN AND EARTH: "I WILL MAKE YOU SWEAR BY THE LORD, GOD OF HEAVEN AND GOD OF EARTH" (Genesis 24:3). ({SP_(313, 3, "לא", "היה", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא", "מלך", "אלא")} "the Holy One, blessed be He, was king only"; {SP_(313, 3, "המליכו", "על", "השמים", "ועל", "הארץ")} "he made Him king over the heavens and over the earth"): THE TWO TITLES OF GENESIS 24 read as before and after Abraham (the tape\'s own entries — RUN CITATIONS); the compile: no law — a status of the Name\'s reach (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE KEPT HIM AS THE APPLE OF HIS EYE" — HAD THE HOLY ONE ASKED ABRAHAM FOR HIS EYEBALL HE WOULD HAVE GIVEN IT, AND NOT HIS EYEBALL ONLY BUT HIS SOUL, DEAREST OF ALL: "TAKE NOW YOUR SON, YOUR ONLY ONE (yechidekha), ISAAC" (Genesis 22:2) — IS IT NOT KNOWN HE WAS HIS ONLY SON? RATHER THIS IS THE SOUL CALLED THE ONLY ONE: "DELIVER MY SOUL FROM THE SWORD, MY ONLY ONE FROM THE DOG" (Psalm 22:21). ({SP_(313, 4, "אפלו", "בקש", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא", "מאברהם", "אבינו")} "even had the Holy One, blessed be He, asked of Abraham our father"; {SP_(313, 4, "אלא", "זו", "נפש", "שנקראת", "יחידה")} "rather this is the soul that is called the only one"): the binding\'s "only one" read as the soul (Genesis 22:2 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION; the Writings\' seat cited); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "HE FOUND HIM IN A DESERT LAND" — THESE ARE ISRAEL: "LIKE GRAPES IN THE WILDERNESS I FOUND ISRAEL" (Hosea 9:10). ({SP_(313, 5, "אלו", "ישראל")} "these are Israel"): the second reading opens — Israel found (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IN THE WASTE, A HOWLING WILDERNESS" — IN A PLACE OF TROUBLES, OF RAIDERS, OF BANDITS. ({SP_(313, 6, "במקום", "הצרות", "במקום", "הגיסות", "במקום", "הלסטים")} "in a place of troubles, of raiders, of bandits"): the desert\'s three dangers (the parable\'s words at 313:1 repeated); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE COMPASSED HIM ABOUT" — BEFORE MOUNT SINAI: "AND YOU SHALL SET BOUNDS FOR THE PEOPLE ROUND ABOUT, SAYING" (Exodus 19:12). ({SP_(313, 7, "לפני", "הר", "סיני")} "before Mount Sinai"): the compassing Sinai\'s bounds (Exodus 19:12 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE CARED FOR HIM" — WITH THE TEN UTTERANCES: IT TEACHES THAT WHEN THE UTTERANCE WENT OUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE ISRAEL SAW IT AND UNDERSTOOD IT, AND KNEW HOW MUCH MIDRASH (EXPOSITION) IS IN IT, HOW MUCH LAW, HOW MANY A-FORTIORI ARGUMENTS, HOW MANY VERBAL ANALOGIES. ({SP_(313, 8, "בעשרת", "הדברות")} "with the ten utterances"; {SP_(313, 8, "וכמה", "קלים", "וחמורים", "יש", "בו")} "and how many a-fortiori arguments are in it"; {SP_(313, 8, "וכמה", "גזרות", "שוות", "יש", "בו")} "and how many verbal analogies are in it"): THE MIDDOT SEEN IN THE UTTERANCE — the a-fortiori (I1) and the verbal analogy (I2) NAMED as contents of each of the ten words (the Mekhilta on Exodus 20:15 the parallel, cited): the compile rules present in the program at its giving — the tradition\'s own statement of THE COMPILER LAW; no argument by a middah here (the codes named, not typed as an argument); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE KEPT HIM AS THE APPLE OF HIS EYE" — THEY WENT BACK TWELVE MIL AND RETURNED TWELVE MIL AT EVERY UTTERANCE, AND WERE NOT DAUNTED BY THE VOICES NOR BY THE TORCHES. ({SP_(313, 9, "הולכים", "שנים", "עשר", "מיל", "וחוזרים", "שנים", "עשר")} "they went twelve mil and returned twelve mil"): the twelve mil of the camp (Tosefta Arakhin 1:10 the testing shelf, cited by the translator; the camp\'s size the answer sheet\'s number); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "HE FOUND HIM IN A DESERT LAND" — EVERYTHING WAS FOUND AND SUPPLIED TO THEM IN THE DESERT: THE WELL RISING FOR THEM, THE MANNA COMING DOWN, THE QUAIL AT HAND, THE CLOUDS OF GLORY ROUND ABOUT; "AND IN THE WASTE, A HOWLING WILDERNESS" — IN A PLACE OF TROUBLES, OF RAIDERS, OF BANDITS. ({SP_(313, 10, "הכל", "מצוי", "ומספק", "להם", "במדבר")} "everything found and supplied to them in the desert"; {SP_(313, 10, "באר", "עולה", "להם", "מן", "יורד", "להם")} "the well rising for them, the manna coming down for them"): THE DESERT\'S GIFTS — the well, the manna, the quail, the clouds (305:3\'s three gifts of the three righteous, sitting 19; the daemon of the three gifts the debt carried to 34:5): Onkelos\'s "He supplied their needs" (32:10) is this row\'s reading (the measure); the tape\'s own entries (Exodus 16, Numbers 11, 20 — RUN CITATIONS); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE COMPASSED HIM ABOUT" — WITH BANNERS: THREE FROM THE NORTH, THREE FROM THE SOUTH, THREE FROM THE EAST, THREE FROM THE WEST. ({SP_(313, 11, "בדגלים", "שלשה", "מן", "הצפון", "שלשה", "מן", "הדרום")} "with banners: three from the north, three from the south"): the camp of Numbers 2 (three tribes a side — the tape\'s own count, a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE CARED FOR HIM" — WITH TWO GIFTS: WHEN ONE OF THE NATIONS STRETCHED HIS HAND TO GATHER OF THE MANNA NOTHING CAME UP IN HIS HAND; TO DRAW WATER FROM THE WELL — NOTHING CAME UP IN HIS HAND. ({SP_(313, 12, "בשתי", "מתנות")} "with two gifts"; {SP_(313, 12, "לא", "היה", "עולה", "בידו", "כלום")} "nothing came up in his hand"): the manna and the well Israel\'s alone; no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE KEPT HIM AS THE APPLE OF HIS EYE" — AS IT SAYS "RISE UP, O LORD, AND LET YOUR ENEMIES BE SCATTERED, LET THOSE WHO HATE YOU FLEE BEFORE YOU" (Numbers 10:35). ({SP_(313, 13, "יצרנהו", "כאישון", "עינו")} "He kept him as the apple of His eye"): the ark\'s song the guard (Numbers 10:35 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "HE FOUND HIM IN A DESERT LAND" — THIS IS THE TIME TO COME: "THEREFORE, BEHOLD, I WILL ALLURE HER AND BRING HER INTO THE WILDERNESS AND SPEAK TO HER HEART" (Hosea 2:16). ({SP_(313, 14, "זה", "לעתיד", "לבוא")} "this is the time to come"): the fourth reading — the desert of the future (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(313, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IN THE WASTE, A HOWLING WILDERNESS" — THESE ARE THE FOUR KINGDOMS: "WHO LED YOU THROUGH THE GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS" (8:15). ({SP_(313, 15, "אלו", "ארבע", "מלכיות")} "these are the four kingdoms"): 8:15\'s wilderness the four kingdoms (the seat that read this row at chapter 8); no law (DV32-04). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 8\'s reading — 8:15).')
srow(313, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE COMPASSED HIM ABOUT" — WITH ELDERS; "HE CARED FOR HIM" — WITH PROPHETS; "HE KEPT HIM AS THE APPLE OF HIS EYE" — HE GUARDS THEM FROM THE HARMFUL SPIRITS THAT THEY HARM THEM NOT: "FOR HE WHO TOUCHES YOU TOUCHES THE APPLE OF HIS EYE" (Zechariah 2:12). ({SP_(313, 16, "בזקנים", "יבוננהו", "בנביאים")} "with elders; He cared for him — with prophets"; {SP_(313, 16, "משמרם", "מן", "המזיקים", "שלא", "יזיקום")} "He guards them from the harmful spirits that they harm them not"): the last row of the piska — the three verbs in the future; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(314, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS AN EAGLE STIRS UP HER NEST" (32:11) — THIS EAGLE DOES NOT ENTER ITS NEST AT ONCE BUT BEATS ITS YOUNG WITH ITS WINGS, BETWEEN TREE AND TREE, BETWEEN BOOTH AND BOOTH, THAT THEY WAKE AND HAVE STRENGTH TO RECEIVE IT; SO WHEN THE HOLY ONE WAS REVEALED TO GIVE THE TORAH TO ISRAEL HE WAS NOT REVEALED FROM ONE DIRECTION BUT FROM FOUR: "THE LORD CAME FROM SINAI AND ROSE FROM SEIR TO THEM" (33:2), AND THE FOURTH? "GOD COMES FROM TEMAN" (Habakkuk 3:3). The head row of piska 314 ({SP_(314, 1, "מה", "נשר", "זה", "אין", "נכנס", "לקנו", "מיד")} "this eagle does not enter its nest at once"; {SP_(314, 1, "לא", "נגלה", "עליהם", "מרוח", "אחת", "אלא", "מארבע")} "He was not revealed to them from one direction but from four"): THE EAGLE THE GIVING — the four directions of the revelation (33:2 ahead, cited by the row and not read — the blessing\'s chapter; the Mekhilta of R. Shimon the parallel); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(314, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SPREADS ABROAD HER WINGS, TAKES THEM" — AS IT SAYS "AND IN THE WILDERNESS, WHERE YOU SAW HOW THE LORD YOUR GOD CARRIED YOU" (1:31). ({SP_(314, 2, "יפרוש", "כנפיו", "יקחהו")} "He spreads His wings, takes him"): 1:31\'s carrying (the seat that read this row at chapters 1-3 — the tape\'s own entry); no law (DV32-04). REREAD WHOLE (chapters 1-3\'s reading — 1:31).')
srow(314, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEARS THEM ON HER PINIONS" — AS IT SAYS "AND I BORE YOU ON EAGLES\' WINGS" (Exodus 19:4). ({SP_(314, 3, "ישאהו", "על", "אברתו")} "bears him on his pinion"): THE TWIN TAUGHT — Exodus 19:4\'s eagles\' wings (the measure\'s twin by sense with one shared token) paired by the spine itself: the Link Review Law\'s teacher for the eagle (Exodus 19:4 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(314, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AS AN EAGLE STIRS UP HER NEST" — THIS IS THE TIME TO COME: "THE VOICE OF MY BELOVED, BEHOLD HE COMES" (Song of Songs 2:8). ({SP_(314, 4, "זה", "לעתיד", "לבוא")} "this is the time to come"): the eagle of the redemption (the Writings\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(314, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SPREADS ABROAD HER WINGS" — AS IT SAYS "I WILL SAY TO THE NORTH: GIVE UP, AND TO THE SOUTH: KEEP NOT BACK" (Isaiah 43:6). ({SP_(314, 5, "יפרש", "כנפיו")} "He spreads His wings"): the gathering from the four directions (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(314, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEARS THEM ON HER PINIONS" — AS IT SAYS "AND THEY SHALL BRING YOUR SONS IN THEIR BOSOM" (Isaiah 49:22). ({SP_(314, 6, "ישאהו", "על", "אברתו")} "bears him on his pinion"): the last row of the piska — the nations carrying Israel home (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE LORD ALONE DID LEAD HIM" (32:12) — THE HOLY ONE SAID TO THEM: AS YOU DWELT ALONE IN THIS WORLD AND HAD NO BENEFIT OF THE NATIONS, SO I WILL SETTLE YOU ALONE IN THE TIME TO COME AND NONE OF THE NATIONS SHALL BENEFIT FROM YOU. The head row of piska 315 ({SP_(315, 1, "כדרך", "שישבתם", "יחידים", "בעולם", "הזה")} "as you dwelt alone in this world"; {SP_(315, 1, "כך", "אני", "עתיד", "להושיב", "אתכם", "יחידים", "לעתיד")} "so I will settle you alone in the future"): ALONE IN BOTH WORLDS — Onkelos\'s future at 32:12 ("the LORD alone is to make them dwell in the world to be renewed" — the measure) is this row\'s reading; the compile: a status of separation (Numbers 23:9\'s "a people dwelling alone" on the tape; 356:5 outside sets the three "alones"); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE WAS NO STRANGE GOD WITH HIM" — THAT NO PRINCE OF THE NATIONS BE PERMITTED TO COME AND RULE OVER YOU: "AND I WENT OUT, AND BEHOLD THE PRINCE OF JAVAN CAME" (Daniel 10:20), "THE PRINCE OF THE KINGDOM OF PERSIA STOOD AGAINST ME" (Daniel 10:13), "BUT I WILL TELL YOU WHAT IS INSCRIBED IN THE WRITING OF TRUTH" (Daniel 10:21). ({SP_(315, 2, "שלא", "תהא", "רשות", "לאחד", "משרי", "האמות")} "that none of the princes of the nations be permitted"): the strange god the nations\' angelic prince (the Writings\' seats cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THE LORD ALONE DID LEAD HIM" — I WILL SETTLE YOU AS HEIRS FROM ONE END OF THE WORLD TO THE OTHER: "FROM THE EAST SIDE TO THE WEST SIDE, ASHER ONE" (Ezekiel 48:2), "REUBEN ONE" (48:6), "JUDAH ONE" (48:7) — WHY "ASHER ONE, REUBEN ONE, JUDAH ONE"? ISRAEL WILL TAKE THE LENGTH FROM EAST TO WEST ON A BREADTH OF TWENTY-FIVE THOUSAND REEDS, THEIR MEASURE SEVENTY-FIVE MIL. ({SP_(315, 3, "עתיד", "אני", "להושיב", "אתכם", "נוחלים")} "I will settle you as heirs"; {SP_(315, 3, "על", "רחב", "עשרים", "וחמשת", "אלפים", "קנים")} "on a breadth of twenty-five thousand reeds"; {SP_(315, 3, "שעורם", "שבעים", "וחמשה", "מיל")} "their measure seventy-five mil"): THE FUTURE TRIBAL STRIPS — Ezekiel 48\'s "one" read as a strip across the whole breadth; twenty-five thousand reeds = seventy-five mil (the shelf\'s own conversion — a reed to a mil parameter the compile may register; the Prophets\' seats cited, never read); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE WAS NO STRANGE GOD WITH HIM" — THAT THERE BE AMONG YOU NONE WHO SERVE STRANGE WORSHIP: "THEREFORE BY THIS SHALL THE INIQUITY OF JACOB BE EXPIATED" (Isaiah 27:9). ({SP_(315, 4, "שלא", "יהו", "בכם", "בני", "אדם", "עובדים", "עבודה")} "that there be among you no men who serve worship"): no idolater among the future Israel (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); the compile: the idolatry prohibition\'s status on the tape; no new law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THE LORD ALONE DID LEAD HIM (yanchenu)" — I WILL SETTLE YOU IN REST OF SPIRIT (nachat ruach) IN THE WORLD. ({SP_(315, 5, "עתיד", "אני", "להושיב", "אתכם", "בנחת", "רוח", "בעולם")} "I will settle you in rest of spirit in the world"): the verb read by its root (n-ch — rest); no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(315, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE WAS NO STRANGE GOD WITH HIM" — THAT THERE BE AMONG YOU NONE BUSIED WITH ANY TRADE: "LET THERE BE A HANDFUL OF GRAIN IN THE LAND" (Psalm 72:16) — THE WHEAT SHALL YIELD LOAVES THE FILL OF THIS PALM; "ITS FRUIT SHALL RUSTLE LIKE LEBANON" — THE WHEAT SHALL RUB GRAIN ON GRAIN AND SHED ITS FINE FLOUR ON THE LAND, AND YOU COME AND TAKE A PALMFUL AND HAVE YOUR LIVELIHOOD. ({SP_(315, 6, "שלא", "יהיו", "בכם", "בני", "אדם", "עסוקים", "בפרקמטיא")} "that there be among you no men busied with trade"; {SP_(315, 6, "מלא", "פסת", "יד")} "the fill of a palm"): the last row of the piska — the strange god read as commerce, the future without trade; the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-04). Fresh.')
srow(316, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE MADE HIM RIDE ON THE HIGH PLACES OF THE EARTH" (32:13) — THIS IS THE LAND OF ISRAEL, HIGHER THAN ALL LANDS: "LET US GO UP AT ONCE AND POSSESS IT" (Numbers 13:30), "AND THEY WENT UP AND SPIED OUT THE LAND", "AND THEY WENT UP INTO THE SOUTH AND CAME TO HEBRON" (Numbers 13:21-22), "AND THEY WENT UP OUT OF EGYPT" (Genesis 45:25). The head row of piska 316 ({SP_(316, 1, "זו", "ארץ", "ישראל", "שגבוהה", "מכל", "הארצות")} "this is the land of Israel, higher than all lands"): THE LAND\'S HEIGHT from the verb "go up" (Numbers 13:21-30 and Genesis 45:25 the tape\'s own entries — RUN CITATIONS; Onkelos: the strongholds of the land); no law (DV32-05). Fresh.')
srow(316, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE ATE THE FRUITAGE OF THE FIELD" — THESE ARE THE FRUITS OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL, LIGHTER TO EAT THAN THE FRUITS OF ALL LANDS. ({SP_(316, 2, "אלו", "פרות", "ארץ", "ישראל")} "these are the fruits of the land of Israel"; {SP_(316, 2, "שהם", "קלים", "לאכל")} "that are light to eat"): no law (DV32-05). Fresh.')
srow(316, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE MADE HIM SUCK HONEY OUT OF THE CRAG" — AS SIKHNIN AND ITS NEIGHBORS: IT HAPPENED THAT R. YEHUDAH SAID TO HIS SON, GO AND BRING ME DRIED FIGS FROM THE JAR; HE SAID: FATHER, IT IS OF HONEY; HE SAID: SINK YOUR HAND INTO IT AND YOU WILL BRING UP FIGS FROM IT. ({SP_(316, 3, "כגון", "סכני", "וחברותיה")} "as Sikhnin and its neighbors"; {SP_(316, 3, "אבא", "של", "דבש", "היא")} "father, it is of honey"): the honey of the figs, the Galilee\'s village named — the crag\'s honey the fig\'s (the compile: no law; the land\'s produce a status) (DV32-05). Fresh.')
srow(316, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OIL OUT OF THE FLINTY ROCK" — THESE ARE THE OLIVES OF GUSH CHALAV: IT HAPPENED THAT R. YOSE SAID TO HIS SON IN SEPPHORIS, GO UP AND BRING US OLIVES FROM THE LOFT; HE WENT AND FOUND THE LOFT AFLOAT WITH OIL. ({SP_(316, 4, "אלו", "זיתים", "של", "גוש", "חלב")} "these are the olives of Gush Chalav"; {SP_(316, 4, "ומצא", "את", "העליה", "שצפה", "בשמן")} "and found the loft afloat with oil"): the last row of the piska — the flint\'s oil the olive\'s (Gush Chalav named); no law (DV32-05). Fresh.')
